   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the civil service law, in relation to granting salary\nprotection for provisional and temporary employees",
    "basePrintNo": "S8210",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S8210-2021",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §121, Civ Serv L",
    "lawSection": "Civil Service Law",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S8210\n\nSPONSOR: JACKSON\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the civil service law, in relation to granting salary\nprotection for provisional and temporary employees\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nThis bill would grant salary protection to provisional and temporary\nincumbents and to provide salary protection to permanent incumbents who\ntake a lateral transfer.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1 amends paragraph (a) of subdivision 2 of Section 121 of the\nCivil Service Law to extend its salary protection to provisional and\ntemporary incumbents, as well as to permanent incumbents at the same\ngrade, upon transfer to other positions, by reason of reclassification\nor reallocation.\n\nSection 2 is the effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nMany state employees spend years and, in some cases, their entire\ncareers, in positions considered to be provisional or temporary. When\naction initiated by the Department of Civil Service to maintain salary\nequity among titles results in lowering the grade of a title, permanent\nincumbents are currently granted salary protection as long as they\nretain such position. This bill would increase career mobility by\nexpanding that salary protection to provisional and temporary employees,\nas well as granting permanent incumbents this protection when trans-\nferring to lateral positions.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\n2019-2020: S.6218 - Referred to Civil Service and Pensions/A.7781 -\nReferred to Governmental Employees\n\n \nSTATE AND LOCAL FISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
